                        "sense_id": "0401444f-63a5-3f38-8051-a2150a425ca8",
                        "entry_id": "33d3b979-a0ea-3292-8b60-77d0004670dc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dativ von wer"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e461410e-022a-47e1-82bb-71ce1625c537",
                                "sense_id": "0401444f-63a5-3f38-8051-a2150a425ca8",
                                "text": "Wem soll ich helfen?"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0e453ac9-5ea0-4fdc-94f5-2fb1578c5adb",
                        "source_entry_id": "33d3b979-a0ea-3292-8b60-77d0004670dc",
                        "source_sense_id": "0401444f-63a5-3f38-8051-a2150a425ca8",
                        "source_sense_description": "Dativ von wer",
                        "target_lang_word": "whom",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "whom",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36caa3f3-3012-3c0c-a0c4-cc9bed1731c6",
                                        "entry_id": "bf403a14-7a38-30bb-b426-7a2da318c519",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "What person or people; which person or people.",
                                            "As the object of a verb."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal",
                                            "interrogative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a36d711f-8e18-4f88-835e-20488324e78a",
                                                "sense_id": "36caa3f3-3012-3c0c-a0c4-cc9bed1731c6",
                                                "text": "Whom did you ask?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1d61ba6-277d-4624-a446-ddab61d80519",
                                                "sense_id": "36caa3f3-3012-3c0c-a0c4-cc9bed1731c6",
                                                "text": "“Oh?” she said. “So you have decided to revise my guest list for me? You have the nerve, the – the –” I saw she needed helping out. “Audacity,” I said, throwing her the line. “The audacity to dictate to me who I shall have in my house.” It should have been “whom”, but I let it go. “You have the –” “Crust.” “– the immortal rind,” she amended, and I had to admit it was stronger, “to tell me whom” – she got it right that time – “I may entertain at Brinkley Court and who” – wrong again – “I may not.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7bd58fc0-7446-3701-8161-942d7955837b",
                                        "entry_id": "bf403a14-7a38-30bb-b426-7a2da318c519",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "What person or people; which person or people.",
                                            "As the object of a preposition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal",
                                            "interrogative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c49d09b7-5210-48a3-9429-579a1852ba9b",
                                                "sense_id": "7bd58fc0-7446-3701-8161-942d7955837b",
                                                "text": "To whom are you referring?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88fbd562-0451-4b6c-b403-00049a5a8ebb",
                                                "sense_id": "7bd58fc0-7446-3701-8161-942d7955837b",
                                                "text": "With whom were you talking?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f71d3bd-4f40-42a3-8f36-019d4c09f892",
                                                "sense_id": "7bd58fc0-7446-3701-8161-942d7955837b",
                                                "text": "The stories did not seem to me to touch life. They were plainly intended to have a bracing moral effect, and perhaps had this result for the people at whom they were aimed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41930f8a-eb13-4c0b-aa04-7577e6109dfe",
                                                "sense_id": "7bd58fc0-7446-3701-8161-942d7955837b",
                                                "text": "He read the letter aloud. Sophia listened with the studied air of one for whom, even in these days, a title possessed some surreptitious allurement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "188fcfae-e985-4707-9d07-b7f1b4ab7b16",
                                                "sense_id": "7bd58fc0-7446-3701-8161-942d7955837b",
                                                "text": "“A very hearty pip-pip to you, old ancestor,” I said, well pleased, for she is a woman with whom it is always a privilege to chew the fat. “And a rousing toodle-oo to you, you young blot on the landscape,” she replied cordially."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26589dd5-35d5-4b81-9959-f689268e13eb",
                                                "sense_id": "7bd58fc0-7446-3701-8161-942d7955837b",
                                                "text": "The principal economic activity is copra production, the Government copra plantation covering some 5,170 ha. The population in 1989 was estimated at 2,000, the great majority of whom live in London, Banana and Poland villages in the west."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08464c6b-2a69-39e9-abb3-c1bd4f507185",
                                        "entry_id": "bf403a14-7a38-30bb-b426-7a2da318c519",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used to refer to a previously mentioned person or people."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal",
                                            "relative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c58487d-8a8d-4375-ac37-7bd7dd0c2165",
                                                "sense_id": "08464c6b-2a69-39e9-abb3-c1bd4f507185",
                                                "text": "There is a new girl in the class whom I consider to be a wunderkind."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0bedfcd7-9d75-47f3-8eed-755b967617b9",
                                                "sense_id": "08464c6b-2a69-39e9-abb3-c1bd4f507185",
                                                "text": "She felt miserable unless she had neighbors with whom to quarrel regularly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ff6e0b7-3efe-4731-9df1-fd80f0885732",
                                                "sense_id": "08464c6b-2a69-39e9-abb3-c1bd4f507185",
                                                "text": "We have ten employees, half of whom are carpenters. (non-defining)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de8ce7cc-0502-4448-9425-5e5067d30e5a",
                                                "sense_id": "08464c6b-2a69-39e9-abb3-c1bd4f507185",
                                                "text": "That is the woman whom I spoke to earlier. (defining)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7bd1727d-6ead-43e9-b043-c97cc80d9b72",
                                                "sense_id": "08464c6b-2a69-39e9-abb3-c1bd4f507185",
                                                "text": "Mr Smith, whom we all know well, will be giving the speech. (non-defining)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "740a1410-8402-4ab4-92b1-037a83309e17",
                                                "sense_id": "08464c6b-2a69-39e9-abb3-c1bd4f507185",
                                                "text": "He's a person with whom I work (defining)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2959070d-980f-46d2-97de-6ab080854d0d",
                                                "sense_id": "08464c6b-2a69-39e9-abb3-c1bd4f507185",
                                                "text": "“Anthea hasn't a notion in her head but to vamp a lot of silly mugwumps. She's set her heart on that tennis bloke[…]whom the papers are making such a fuss about.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e66e96a1-b05b-474a-a71e-1a3583c35fed",
                                                "sense_id": "08464c6b-2a69-39e9-abb3-c1bd4f507185",
                                                "text": "The eminent brain specialist to whom she alluded was a man I would not have cared to lunch with myself, our relations having been on the stiff side since the night at Lady Wickham's place in Hertfordshire when, acting on the advice of my hostess's daughter Roberta, I had punctured his hot-water bottle with a darning needle in the small hours of the morning. Quite unintentional, of course."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dee6d669-92c4-4782-8acf-c60426f02f67",
                                                "sense_id": "08464c6b-2a69-39e9-abb3-c1bd4f507185",
                                                "text": "A woman shooting pool whom you know has red hair even though the photograph is black and white."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1ab5be51-9563-3a6a-9226-a107a74f9368",
                                        "entry_id": "bf403a14-7a38-30bb-b426-7a2da318c519",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The person(s) whom; whomever."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6018ccbf-9640-4974-95ad-2dd514111fa3",
                                                "sense_id": "1ab5be51-9563-3a6a-9226-a107a74f9368",
                                                "text": "To whom it may concern, all business of John Smith Ltd. has now been transferred to Floggitt & Runne."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60035437-3d50-3d1d-9ab2-99f10c71368c",
                                        "entry_id": "bf403a14-7a38-30bb-b426-7a2da318c519",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Also used with names of collective nouns that are groups of people, especially singularly-named musical groups or sports teams."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55b6f813-eeb4-470e-8477-bdedbefe5a78",
                                                "sense_id": "60035437-3d50-3d1d-9ab2-99f10c71368c",
                                                "text": "Whom was Lemmy bassist for? Motörhead!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
